on-arrival: {!
Q.psr_support_maisky = 0;
if (Q.rsdrp_candidate == "Radchenko") {
    if (Q.psr_relation >= 60 || (Q.psr_relation > 40 && Q.psr_party_leader == "Avksentyev")) {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 1;
    } else if (Q.psr_relation <= 40) {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 0;
    } else {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 2;
    }
} else {
    if (Q.psr_relation >= 55 || (Q.psr_relation > 35 && Q.psr_party_leader == "Avksentyev")) {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 1;
    } else if (Q.psr_relation <= 35) {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 0;
    } else {
        Q.psr_support_maisky = 2;
    }
}
!}
max-visits: 1
go-to: psr_failed if psr_support_maisky = 0 or (psr_support_maisky == 2 and historical_mode); psr_success if psr_support_maisky = 1; psr_partial if psr_support_maisky = 2 and not historical_mode

We implore the Socialist-Revolutionary Party to support [+ rsdrp_candidate +]. We attempt to convince them of the necessity for unity in the face of fascism: that if we were divided, we would fall to the Solidarists. [? if psr_relation >= 50 : We also remind them of the history of cooperation between our parties, dating back to 1918. ?]

@psr_failed
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

Unfortunately, the Socialist-Revolutionary Party is not convinced. [? if rsdrp_candidate = "Radchenko" : The Catholics are not impressed with Lyubov Radchenko. This is in part because she is a woman, in part because she had a divorce. ?]

@psr_success
on-arrival: psr_candidate = rsdrp_candidate; Shingarev_bonus += 2.5 if psr_relation < 40
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

The Socialist-Revolutionary Party is convinced! They will be supporting [+ rsdrp_candidate +] for the election.

[? if psr_relation < 40 : Unfortunately, the BVP is breaking with the PSR on this election, supporting Shingarev of the VS instead.  ?]

@psr_partial

The PSR are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @pay_psr: Give them the resources they need.
- @r1_menu: Forget about the PSR.
- @r2_campaigning: Forget about the PSR.

@pay_psr
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 2; psr_candidate = rsdrp_candidate
go-to: r1_menu if round = 0; r2_campaigning if round > 0

With our resources, the PSR are convinced to support [+ rsdrp_candidate +]. Viktor Chernov will drop out of the race.

