@leuchtenberg_victory
on-arrival: chancellor = "Leuchtenberg"; chancellor_party = "NTS"

With [+ nts_candidate +]'s victory, the Solidarists waste no time in consolidating power. [? if president = "Baidalakov": His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint Leuchtenberg as chancellor, first undoing his deportation. ?][? if president = "Leuchtenberg": His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint himself chancellor, using his stormtroopers to attack any opposition. ?]

- @leuchtenberg_takes_power: What next?
- @leuchtenberg_constitutional: This is unconstitutional!

@shingarev_victory
on-arrival: chancellor = "Leuchtenberg"; chancellor_party = "NTS"

With Shingarev's victory, the balance of power passes to the Solidarists. [? if leuchtenberg_deported: His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint Sergey Leuchtenberg as chancellor, first undoing his deportation. ?][? if not leuchtenberg_deported: His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint Sergey Leuchtenberg as chancellor. ?]

- @leuchtenberg_takes_power: What next?
- @leuchtenberg_constitutional: This is blatantly unconstitutional!

@leuchtenberg_constitutional
view-if: presidential_powers

We have passed a constitutional amendment preventing the president from having the power to arbitrarily dismiss a government. To undo this, the far right has called a plebiscite on a new constitutional amendment. Stormtroopers are in the streets, "convincing" voters to support their proposal. Germany is nearing civil war.

- @fight: We will fight the Solidarists in the streets!
- @defeat_democratic: We can only defeat the Solidarists through democratic means!

@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @defeat_democratic: It is not too late to fight constitutionally.

@defeat_democratic
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_democracy_votes = Q.rsdrp_votes + Q.musavat_votes + Q.psr_votes - (Q.sa_strength*Q.sa_militancy/10) + (Q.rb_strength*Q.rb_militancy/10);
if (Q.pro_republic >= 60) {
    Q.pro_democracy_votes += Q.rkp_votes;
    Q.pro_democracy_votes += Q.kadets_votes;
}
!}
go-to: ref_win if pro_democracy_votes >= 50; ref_lose if pro_democracy_votes < 50

@ref_win
on-arrival: constitutional_crisis = 1

Despite the Solidarist threats, supporters of the RSDRP and the democratic parties refuse to turn out for the referendum, depriving it of the necessary threshold to pass. This is a small victory, as stormtroopers still run rampant in the streets. There is no constitutional path to absolute power, but will that stop the Solidarists? 

- @game_over: The ending is yet to be seen...

@ref_lose

- @leuchtenberg_takes_power: What next?


@election_end
go-to: nabokov_win if winner = "Nabokov"; radchenko_win if winner = "Radchenko"; bundesrepublik_win if winner = "Yakubovich" or winner = "Chernov"; leuchtenberg_victory if winner = "Leuchtenberg" or winner = "Baidalakov" or winner = "Baidalakov"; shingarev_victory if winner = "Shingarev"; milyutin_victory if winner = "Milyutin" or winner = "Milyutin"; kalinin_victory if winner = "Kalinin" or winner = "Kalinin"; nazis_lose if winner = "Maisky" or winner = "Rasulzade"; cultural_victory if winner = "Zaslavsky" or winner = "Gorky"; pavlov_victory if winner = "Pavlov"
on-arrival: president = winner; president = "Kalinin" if president == "Kalinin"; president = "Milyutin" if president = "Milyutin"; president = "Baidalakov" if president = "Baidalakov"

The election has been won by [+ winner_desc +].

@kalinin_victory
go-to: kalinin_democrat if presidential_powers; kalinin_civil_war if not presidential_powers

@kalinin_civil_war
on-arrival: rkp_relation = 80

# TODO: depose the chancellor?

Kalinin wastes no time in consolidating power, using all means available to reshape the government. In response, the far-right immediately launches a coup attempt. We have no choice but to unite with the RKP against the Solidarists...

- @civil_war: This is civil war.

@kalinin_democrat

Despite the victory of the anti-constitutionalist Kalinin, he appears to be respecting the constitutional constraints on presidential power, at least for now. There is no appetite on the right for a coup at this moment. The bourgeoisie have to live with a communist president, at least for now.


@milyutin_victory
achievement: rote_millionar
go-to: nazis_lose

The bourgeois and right-wing parties are up in arms about the prospect of a Communist president, although Milyutin and the RKP conciliators take pains to assure Germany of their commitment to the democratic republic. There is no energy for a coup against the new president. The bourgeoisie will have to live with whatever comes.

@nabokov_win
achievement: zeppelin_kapitan
go-to: nazis_lose


@radchenko_win
achievement: wahlrechts
go-to: nazis_lose

This is a historic victory - Lyubov Radchenko is the first woman to be elected president in any republic, anywhere in the world.

@pavlov_victory
achievement: republik_der_wissenschaft
go-to: nazis_lose

@cultural_victory
go-to: nazis_lose



@bundesrepublik_win
go-to: bundesrepublik_achieve if presidential_powers; nazis_lose if not presidential_powers

@bundesrepublik_achieve
achievement: bundesrepublik
go-to: nazis_lose

@nazis_lose

After its electoral defeat, the NTS-VS coalition is collapsing into infighting and financial insolvency. The far-right's moment has seemingly ended, at least for now.
